# Fetched product pages. Derived data, per-machine, and about 250 MB after a full
# --browserbase run at ~450 KB a page — git is the wrong place for it. Deleting the
# directory costs nothing but a re-fetch.
.page-cache/

# Generated by build_prebake.py. The manifest and images ARE committed today so Ani is
# unblocked, hence no rule here — they move to R2 once that is wired, and this is where the
# ignore goes when they do.

# Catalogue run output. .bulk/ holds a full copy of every merchant catalogue crawled and
# .load/ the SQL and upload script generated from it — both regenerable from the merchant
# list, both far too large and too churny for git.
.bulk/
.load/
